{"id": 10, "ts": 1784068957.555977, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I appreciate Anna\u2019s focus on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s technical strengths, but I remain less convinced that those outweigh the crew\u2011cooperation concerns.\u202fCandidate\u202fC\u2019s unfriendly demeanor and the note that they are \u201cnot open to new ideas\u201d raise a clear risk to constructive cockpit communication, and their unhealthy eating habit could affect long\u2011haul reliability.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB demonstrates the core safety pillars we need: very conscientious (operational reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), and excels at assessing weather and computer\u2011based systems (technical competence).\u202fWhile the feedback about \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and a pretentious tone signals a communication weakness, it is a single\u2011point issue that can be addressed through targeted crew\u2011resource\u2011training, whereas C\u2019s interpersonal style appears more ingrained.\u202fGiven the priority of reliability, stress handling, and technical decision\u2011making for long\u2011distance flights, I would provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fB, provided we commit to a focused communication\u2011coaching plan."}
