{"id": 13, "ts": 1784068973.1557074, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I appreciate Sofia\u2019s and Markus\u2019s points about the critical importance of reliability and stress resilience for long\u2011haul operations. Candidate\u202fB\u2019s very conscientious nature gives us 100\u202f% operational reliability, and his proven ability to handle stress well directly addresses the stress\u2011resilience criterion. His strong weather\u2011assessment skill and excellent computer abilities further support the technical and cognitive competence we need. While his \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and occasional pretentious tone are concerns, these are communication issues that can be mitigated through targeted crew\u2011resource\u2011training, as you both noted. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC, despite impressive anticipation and spatial vision, shows a pattern of unfriendly, \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d behaviour and resistance to criticism, which threatens crew cooperation and cockpit communication\u2014areas that are far harder to remediate. Given the balance of strengths and addressable weaknesses, I now align with the panel\u2019s emerging view and provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fB."}
